      "text": "The bug is that `partial_trace` expects integer qubit indices, but the code passes `QuantumRegister` objects. The fix converts each register into the indices of its qubits in the circuit.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import Aer, QuantumCircuit, QuantumRegister, transpile\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import partial_trace\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit()\nreg1 = QuantumRegister(2)\nqc.add_register(reg1)\nreg2 = QuantumRegister(2)\nqc.add_register(reg2)\nreg3 = QuantumRegister(2)\nqc.add_register(reg3)\nreg4 = QuantumRegister(2)\nqc.add_register(reg4)\n\nqc.h(reg1[0])\nqc.cnot(reg1[0], reg2[0])\nqc.h(reg3[0])\nqc.x(reg4[0])\nqc.cnot(reg3[0], reg4[0])\n\nsimulator = Aer.get_backend(\"aer_simulator\")\nqc.save_statevector()\ntranspiled_qc = transpile(qc, simulator)\nresult = simulator.run(transpiled_qc).result()\n\n# FIX: partial_trace takes integer qubit indices, but registers were passed -> convert each register's qubits to their circuit indices, because partial_trace needs integer positions\ntraced_over_registers = [qc.qubits.index(qubit) for reg in [reg2, reg4] for qubit in reg]\ndensity_matrix = partial_trace(result.get_statevector(), traced_over_registers)\n```",
